    "en": {
      "title": "The Band That Appeared Only in the Rain",
      "location": "Hội An, Vietnam",
      "body": "A sudden rain swept through the market in Hội An.\n\nTourists and shopkeepers rushed beneath the eaves of the yellow buildings.\n\nA wide puddle formed in the market aisle.\n\nLin, who sold fruit, looked up at the sky while shielding her mangoes.\n\n“Looks like that’s it for customers today.”\n\nThe hat seller next door replied:\n\n“Then we’ll have to entertain ourselves.”\n\nHe brought out an old cooking pot and began striking it with a wooden stick.\n\nClonk, clonk, clang.\n\nThe fish seller drummed on an empty foam box.\nThe flower seller rang a metal bucket.\nA girl at the drinks stall shook a bundle of straws.\n\nShaka-shaka-shaka.\n\nNo one knew whether it counted as proper music.\n\nBut mixed with the sound of rain, it became strangely cheerful.\n\nA traveler sheltering under the eaves began to dance.\nBeside him, an elderly woman holding shopping bags started moving her shoulders.\n\nLin picked up a mango and held it like a microphone.\n\n“Today’s special performance. Admission is one smile.”\n\nLaughter rose throughout the market.\n\nThe rain grew heavier.\nThe makeshift band played louder.\n\nPeople trapped by the downpour crowded beneath the eaves.\n\nBefore long, a chorus of voices joined the pots, boxes, and buckets.\n\nBy the time the rain stopped, nearly all of Lin’s mangoes had been sold.\n\n“The power of music,” said the hat seller.\n\nLin shook her head.\n\n“No. They sheltered from the rain for so long that they got hungry.”\n\nThe hat seller turned the wet pot upside down and inspected its dents to see whether it would survive the next storm."
    },
    "zh": {
      "title": "只在雨天出现的乐队",
      "location": "越南·会安",
      "body": "会安的市场突然下起大雨。\n\n游客和摊主纷纷躲到黄色建筑的屋檐下。\n\n市场通道里很快积起一大片水洼。\n\n卖水果的玲一边护着芒果，一边抬头看天。\n\n“今天大概不会再有客人了。”\n\n隔壁卖帽子的老板说：\n\n“那我们自己先热闹起来。”\n\n他从店里搬出一口旧锅，拿木棍敲了起来。\n\n咚、咚、当。\n\n鱼贩敲着空泡沫箱。\n花贩用金属水桶打拍子。\n饮料摊的女孩摇起一捆吸管。\n\n沙沙沙。\n\n这到底算不算音乐，谁也说不准。\n\n可它和雨声混在一起，听着格外欢快。\n\n屋檐下的一名旅行者先跳了起来。\n旁边提着购物袋的老太太，也跟着晃起肩膀。\n\n玲拿起一个芒果，当作麦克风。\n\n“今日特别演出。入场费是一个笑容。”\n\n笑声一下传遍了整个市场。\n\n雨越下越大。\n这支临时乐队也越敲越响。\n\n被大雨困住的人，一个接一个挤到屋檐下。\n\n没过多久，锅、箱子和水桶的声响中，又加入了一大群人的合唱。\n\n等雨停下来，玲的芒果已经卖得差不多了。\n\n“这是音乐的功劳。”\n\n帽子店老板说。\n\n玲摇摇头。\n\n“才不是。他们躲雨躲得太久，肚子饿了。”\n\n帽子店老板把湿漉漉的锅翻过来，认真看了看上面的凹痕，琢磨着下场雨还能不能继续用。"
    }
